commit 143bca5c44bea01187bccf88c930759486a8f6fa
Author: InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
Date:   Wed May 20 02:08:50 2026 -0700

    fix(commands/keychain): enforce KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS at runtime (P0 G2.5)
    
    Why
    - Codex cross-vendor review (P0-2) flagged that `commands/keychain.rs`
      exposed `secret_set` / `secret_get` / `secret_del` without the runtime
      `ensure_*_allowed` window-origin check, while `capabilities/AUDIT.md`
      and `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §6/§7 (added in ad5f1d3)
      explicitly claimed every JS-callable command had one. Result: a
      widget / pet / ai-cube / grid_* window with a mis-attached capability
      could reach the Keychain seam, breaking the G2.5 two-layer invariant
      promised by the docs.
    
    What
    - Add `KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS: &[&str] = &["account", "control"]`
      constant in `commands/keychain.rs` mirroring the existing
      `CRYPTO_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` / `DATABASE_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` pattern.
    - Add `is_keychain_window_allowed(label)` and
      `ensure_keychain_window_allowed(label) -> AppResult<()>` returning
      `AppError::SyncCapabilityDenied(...)` (E3004) on reject.
    - Inject `window: tauri::WebviewWindow` as the FIRST parameter of
      `secret_set` / `secret_get` / `secret_del`; each command now calls
      `ensure_keychain_window_allowed(window.label())?` before any platform
      Keychain access. TS `packages/core-data/src/keychain.ts` is unchanged
      because Tauri's IPC auto-extracts the `window` parameter from the
      request envelope rather than the JS args payload.
    - Add 2 new cargo unit tests:
      - `keychain_allowlist_admits_account_and_control` covers the admit path.
      - `keychain_allowlist_rejects_widget_pet_aicube` covers reject for
        `widget_clock` / `pet` / `ai_cube` / `unknown` / `grid_xxx` / `grid_`
        / `main` / `console` and asserts the error message contains both the
        rejected label and `secret_*`.
    - Update `capabilities/AUDIT.md` row for `secret_*` to name the new
      `KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` constant explicitly (was: "window-origin
      check inside `commands::keychain`").
    - Update `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §6 security rule for
      `secret_*` to mention the runtime `KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` reject
      path and the `E3004` error code.
    - Append 2026-05-20 row to `packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/dev_log.md`
      Work Log documenting the P0-2 fix.
    
    Scope
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/keychain.rs (runtime check + tests),
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md (audit row),
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md (§6 row),
    - packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/dev_log.md (Work Log).
    
    Risk
    - Low. Purely additive defence-in-depth check. Legitimate Keychain
      callers (`account`, `control`) keep their access; only mis-routed
      callers (widget / pet / ai-cube / grid_* / main / console) are now
      rejected at the runtime layer instead of the platform layer. No
      existing TS callers change.
    
    Docs
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md,
      docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md,
      packages/tauri-capability-allowlist/docs/dev_log.md.
    
    Tests
    - cargo check --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml : PASS
    - cargo check --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --features crypto : PASS
    - cargo test --manifest-path apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml keychain:: : 5 tests PASS (2 new + 3 existing platform tests)
    - pnpm --filter @repo/core-data test : 58 tests PASS
    
