     8	- `plugin-data-database.json` — Repository v0 SQLite seam (G2.5 addition).
     9	
    10	## Window scopes
    11	
    12	| Window | Capability files attached | Custom invoke_handler enforcement |
    13	|---|---|---|
    14	| `main` | default, plugin-data-database | host commands; database commands (window-origin check) |
    15	| `control` | default, plugin-account-crypto, plugin-account-keychain, plugin-data-database | all custom commands |
    16	| `grid_*` | default, plugin-data-database | window commands; database commands |
    17	| `account` | plugin-account-crypto, plugin-account-keychain, plugin-data-database | crypto_*, secret_*, db_* |
    18	| `console` | plugin-data-database | db_* via plugin-console (Track B) |
    19	| `widget_*` | (none) | none — widgets must route through their owning plugin |
    20	| `pet` | (none) | none — pet plugin owns its own state via plugin |
    21	| `ai_cube` | (none) | none — AI commands run via control |
    22	
    23	## Surfaced commands and enforcement layers
    24	
    25	| Command | Capability file | Runtime allowlist constant |
    26	|---|---|---|
    27	| `core:window:*`, `core:event:*`, `core:webview:*` | default.json | Tauri permission system |
    28	| `opener:default` | default.json | Tauri plugin |
    29	| `create_grid_window` and siblings | default.json | host validates gridId |
    30	| `crypto_*` | plugin-account-crypto.json | `commands::crypto::CRYPTO_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` (account, control) |
    31	| `secret_set` / `secret_get` / `secret_del` | plugin-account-keychain.json | `commands::keychain::KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` (account, control) |
    32	| `db_init` / `db_put` / `db_get` / `db_list` / `db_delete` | plugin-data-database.json (G2.5) | `commands::database::DATABASE_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` (main, control, account, console) + `grid_*` prefix |
    33	
    34	## Minimization notes
    35	
    36	- `default.json` keeps the `core:window:*` and `core:webview:*` set used by `lib.rs::run()` for the transparent main / control / grid construction; nothing was removed because every entry corresponds to a verified caller.
    37	- `core:event:default` is required by the cross-window event bus (`@repo/core/events`).
    38	- `opener:default` is intentionally retained for user-initiated file/URL openers but should be revisited if plugins start using `tauri-plugin-opener` programmatically; flagged in the audit but kept for now to avoid touching G1.3 path-DnD flows.
    39	- No window outside the allowlist can invoke `db_*` even if a future capability file widens the file scope, because the runtime `ensure_database_window_allowed` check is layered on top of the capability system. The same defence-in-depth pattern is already in place for `crypto_*` and `secret_*`.
